title: The Twenty-One Conditions
subtitle: The Second Congress of the International meets in Moscow.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 7 and crisis = 0 and congress_done = 0 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.congress_done = 1;
RG.news('Second Congress of the International: Zinoviev\'s twenty-one conditions', 3);
!}

= The Twenty-One Conditions

The Second Congress of the Communist International opens in Petrograd on 19 July and moves to Moscow. A map of Poland hangs on the wall of the Kremlin hall, and every morning the delegates watch the red flags move closer to Warsaw. [? if levi_chair = 1 : Paul Levi leads our delegation and sits on the presidium. ?]

The USPD has sent Crispien and Dittmann from its right and Däumig and Stoecker from its left. Zinoviev has drafted the conditions of membership: a centralised party under the Executive, illegal work beside legal work, cells in every union, and the expulsion of "reformists and centrists". Lenin adds one more: whoever votes against the conditions at his own party's congress is to be expelled.

Every section must accept them, ours included.

- @accept: Vote for the conditions as they stand.
- @amend: Accept them, and fight for amendments that keep the door open to the USPD's members.
- @reject: Refuse conditions that let Moscow choose our allies and our leaders.

@accept
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Moscow will be generous.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.twenty_one_conditions = 1;
Q.independence -= 8;
Q.resources += 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 10);
!}

The conditions pass with a handful of votes against. Zinoviev embraces our delegation.

@amend
subtitle: [? if independence >= 45 : We are strong enough to be heard. ?][? if independence < 45 : Zinoviev may not need to listen. ?]
on-arrival: {!
var strong = Q.independence >= 45 && Q.members >= 40;
Q.twenty_one_conditions = strong ? 2 : 1;
if (strong) { Q.uspd_score += 1; RG.ecci('zinoviev', -6); } else { RG.ecci('zinoviev', -3); }
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
!}

[? if twenty_one_conditions = 2 : Our amendments pass in commission. The conditions are to be applied "with regard to national circumstances", and no leader of the USPD left is named for expulsion. Däumig thanks us privately. ?][? if twenty_one_conditions = 1 : Zinoviev listens politely and changes nothing. The conditions pass as drafted, with our votes. ?]

@reject
subtitle: Moscow will cut off the money and look for a new leadership.
on-arrival: {!
Q.twenty_one_conditions = Q.independence >= 65 ? 2 : 3;
Q.independence += 10;
Q.moscow_subsidy = 0;
Q.uspd_score -= 1;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -15);
if (Q.twenty_one_conditions == 2) {
    RG.ledger('The German party forced Moscow to soften the twenty-one conditions.', 'e20_21_softened');
} else {
    RG.ecci('lenin', -8);
    RG.punish('rival');
    RG.ledger('The German party refused the twenty-one conditions.', 'e20_21_refused');
}
!}

[? if twenty_one_conditions = 2 : Lenin himself intervenes, and the conditions are softened for Germany: no names and no deadlines. Zinoviev will remember who embarrassed him. ?][? if twenty_one_conditions = 3 : The conditions pass over our votes. The subsidy stops, and Radek begins talking to our Left about the German leadership. ?]
